        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "It has been reported that the thermal decomposition mechanism of aliphatic–aromatic polyesters such as PET and poly(butylene terephthalate) is a b-CH hydrogen-transfer process via a six-membered ring transition state in the ethylene–ester unit, at which carbon–oxygen bond scission takes place to yield carboxyl and vinyl ester end groups<sup>27–30</sup> [Scheme 2(a)]."
