        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "Montaudo et al.<sup>31</sup> concluded that the primary thermal decomposition process of some aliphatic–aromatic polyamides including poly(ethylene terephthalamide) proceeds via a b-CH hydrogen-transfer process accompanying carbon–nitrogen bond scission in the ethylene–amide unit with the formation of thermal decomposition products having amide and N-vinylamide end groups [Scheme 2(b)]."
